  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Small, professional expeditionary army: 1st (UK) Division light/light-mechanised brigades, 3rd (UK) Division heavy brigades transitioning from Warrior/Challenger 2 to Boxer/Challenger 3/Ajax, 16 Air Assault Brigade, the Ranger Regiment for partner-force work, and Royal Marines commandos for littoral and Arctic raiding. Forward-leaning NATO role in Estonia (Op Cabrit). Long counter-insurgency experience from Northern Ireland, Iraq and Afghanistan.",
    "squad_size": 8,
    "fireteam": "Rifle section of 8: section commander and 2IC each lead a 4-man fireteam (Charlie and Delta) with rifles, UGL, sharpshooter and a GPMG or LMG role; anti-armour (NLAW/ILAW) carried within the section.",
    "tactics": [
      "Section battle drills: win the firefight, fireteam fire-and-manoeuvre, assault in pairs",
      "Aggressive use of UGL and hand grenades in close-quarter clearance; 'pepper-potting' movement",
      "Mounted patrols in Foxhound/Jackal; Jackal used for fast screening and flank security",
      "Commandos: small-boat and helicopter raids, cold-weather operations",
      "Sharpshooters and GPMG as section firepower anchor; snipers at company level",
      "Thorough casualty drills (Team Medic, rapid CASEVAC by Chinook/Merlin)"
    ],
